WEBVTT

00:01:34.080 --> 00:01:35.320
Hello?

00:01:36.150 --> 00:01:38.610
No, I just got out of the bath.

00:01:38.950 --> 00:01:40.270
It's okay.

00:01:41.090 --> 00:01:43.150
Gunma? Yeah.

00:01:44.200 --> 00:01:46.370
Wow, I never knew there was such a place.

00:01:46.370 --> 00:01:49.750
<b>Mt. Akagi</b>

00:01:46.680 --> 00:01:47.770
I'll go!

00:01:47.770 --> 00:01:49.750
I bet it's pretty there in fall.

00:01:50.170 --> 00:01:53.270
Thanks for inviting me, Honoka-chan.

00:02:02.930 --> 00:02:04.740
The line's still busy.

00:02:05.160 --> 00:02:06.250
Jeez...

00:02:06.250 --> 00:02:08.390
Who's she talking to, anyway?

00:02:08.690 --> 00:02:10.560
Yes? Hello?

00:02:11.360 --> 00:02:13.650
Jizoudake at Mt. Akagi?

00:02:13.860 --> 00:02:15.250
That sounds nice.

00:02:15.250 --> 00:02:17.980
That place has a nice view.

00:02:17.990 --> 00:02:20.740
<b>October</b>

00:02:18.600 --> 00:02:20.750
Sorry, though...

00:02:20.750 --> 00:02:24.990
I have to work and study on the weekend.

00:02:26.680 --> 00:02:28.840
The mountains are so far.

00:02:28.840 --> 00:02:31.170
It sucks, but I'm going to have to pass.

00:02:31.820 --> 00:02:34.300
Sounds tough for Kaede-san.

00:02:37.090 --> 00:02:38.680
This is Aoba.

00:02:38.680 --> 00:02:40.300
Oh, Hinata-san.

00:02:40.480 --> 00:02:42.300
Mt. Akagi?

00:02:42.300 --> 00:02:46.270
<i>It's supposed to be as famous 
as Mt. Tanigawa in Gunma.</i>

00:02:46.270 --> 00:02:47.560
That sounds wonderful.

00:02:47.560 --> 00:02:49.440
I'd love to come along.

00:02:49.730 --> 00:02:52.120
The leaves should be turning, too.

00:02:52.120 --> 00:02:53.730
I bet it'll be pretty.

00:02:54.410 --> 00:02:55.770
<i>I can't wait!</i>

00:02:55.770 --> 00:02:57.440
<i>I've never been there before.</i>

00:03:02.730 --> 00:03:04.170
Busy...

00:03:04.170 --> 00:03:07.100
Who's Hinata talking to, anyway?

00:03:07.100 --> 00:03:10.040
Honoka-chan's inviting us out.

00:03:10.510 --> 00:03:14.460
I guess I can talk to her at school tomorrow.

00:03:14.540 --> 00:03:19.470
<b>Two Promises</b>

00:03:20.330 --> 00:03:21.970
It's so cold.

00:03:21.970 --> 00:03:24.230
I hope it'll be spring soon.

00:03:24.230 --> 00:03:27.230
You're getting ahead. It's not even winter yet.

00:03:27.230 --> 00:03:29.230
I can't wait for spring.

00:03:29.230 --> 00:03:30.650
Right, Kasumi-chan?

00:03:31.980 --> 00:03:35.040
Why do you have to wake up when it's morning?

00:03:35.480 --> 00:03:37.530
I want to stay in my bed forever.

00:03:37.530 --> 00:03:40.070
If only humans could hibernate, too.

00:03:40.070 --> 00:03:42.700
Sheesh, get a grip, you two.

00:03:43.770 --> 00:03:44.880
Gunma?

00:03:45.320 --> 00:03:47.380
Honoka-chan invited us.

00:03:47.380 --> 00:03:50.040
She asked if we want to come on Saturday.

00:03:52.180 --> 00:03:54.200
You'll be coming, of course, right?

00:03:54.200 --> 00:03:56.530
Kokona-chan and Kaede-san are invited, too...

00:03:56.530 --> 00:03:58.230
Kaede-san said she has work.

00:03:58.710 --> 00:04:00.190
I can't go, either.

00:04:00.660 --> 00:04:03.020
I'm going to Mt. Akagi on Saturday.

00:04:03.020 --> 00:04:04.340
With Kokona-chan.

00:04:04.670 --> 00:04:06.420
Huh? You are?

00:04:06.420 --> 00:04:08.350
I never heard about this.

00:04:08.500 --> 00:04:11.300
I called you last night, 
but the line was busy.

00:04:11.300 --> 00:04:14.260
Mt. Akagi is in Gunma, too, isn't it?

00:04:14.260 --> 00:04:16.980
Why don't Honoka-chan and I 
go to Mt. Akagi, too, then?

00:04:16.980 --> 00:04:19.110
It's fine. Don't worry about it.

00:04:19.790 --> 00:04:23.280
Honoka-chan might want to 
go somewhere else, too.

00:04:24.000 --> 00:04:27.390
Besides, we don't need to 
be together all the time.

00:04:28.480 --> 00:04:29.610
Morning.

00:04:29.610 --> 00:04:30.620
Morning.

00:04:30.620 --> 00:04:32.010
Morning!

00:04:32.010 --> 00:04:34.000
Did you see the Seibu game yesterday?

00:04:34.620 --> 00:04:37.130
I thought you weren't interested in baseball.

00:04:37.130 --> 00:04:38.960
That's why I didn't watch it.

00:04:38.960 --> 00:04:40.120
Did Seibu win?

00:04:40.120 --> 00:04:42.010
What the heck? You make no sense.

00:04:42.010 --> 00:04:43.930
6-1. Easy win.

00:04:43.930 --> 00:04:45.940
Oh, yeah? That's great!

00:04:48.510 --> 00:04:49.760
<i>Just you?</i>

00:04:49.760 --> 00:04:52.720
Yeah. Everyone else has plans.

00:04:52.720 --> 00:04:54.640
Sorry, Honoka-chan.

00:04:54.800 --> 00:04:56.360
<i>I don't mind.</i>

00:04:56.360 --> 00:04:57.740
<i>See you Saturday, then.</i>

00:04:57.740 --> 00:04:58.630
Okay.

00:05:02.040 --> 00:05:04.470
I want to try grilled manju.

00:05:04.470 --> 00:05:05.770
Me, too.

00:05:05.770 --> 00:05:08.660
We didn't have any when we went to Tanigawa.

00:05:09.060 --> 00:05:10.910
Say hi to Honoka-chan for me.

00:05:10.910 --> 00:05:11.850
Okay.

00:05:12.850 --> 00:05:15.620
Hey, maybe we should go to Mt. Akagi...

00:05:15.620 --> 00:05:18.480
It's fine, forget about it.

00:05:18.480 --> 00:05:19.790
Next time.

00:05:21.120 --> 00:05:22.420
Really?

00:05:26.260 --> 00:05:29.440
<i>Why would you back down so easily?</i>

00:05:29.440 --> 00:05:31.560
<i>You could have pushed a </i>little<i> more.</i>

00:05:31.560 --> 00:05:32.790
I want to go to Mt. Akagi!

00:05:32.790 --> 00:05:34.300
I want to go! I want to go!

00:05:34.300 --> 00:05:36.060
Oh, fine.

00:05:36.060 --> 00:05:37.310
All right!

00:05:37.480 --> 00:05:39.350
<i>And I would have said okay.</i>

00:05:39.860 --> 00:05:42.580
<i>Something's up with Hinata.</i>

00:05:42.580 --> 00:05:44.190
<i>What's gotten into her?</i>

00:05:50.680 --> 00:05:52.350
Are you leaving early tomorrow?

00:05:52.350 --> 00:05:55.050
Higahan at 5:19, I think.

00:05:55.050 --> 00:05:56.050
That's early!

00:05:56.050 --> 00:05:58.200
I'll be at 7:21.

00:05:58.200 --> 00:05:59.260
When are you going home?

00:05:59.260 --> 00:06:00.540
Dunno.

00:06:00.540 --> 00:06:01.810
I figured.

00:06:01.810 --> 00:06:04.480
I don't think it'll be too late.

00:06:04.480 --> 00:06:06.510
It'll be nice if we can go home together.

00:06:06.510 --> 00:06:07.570
Yeah.

00:06:10.550 --> 00:06:11.760
I'll talk to you later.

00:06:11.760 --> 00:06:12.300
Okay.

00:06:22.820 --> 00:06:24.110
Hinata-san!

00:06:24.110 --> 00:06:25.370
Good morning!

00:06:25.370 --> 00:06:26.880
Morning.

00:06:26.880 --> 00:06:28.190
It's still pitch-black out.

00:06:28.190 --> 00:06:29.100
Yes.

00:06:29.100 --> 00:06:31.490
It's kind of exciting.

00:06:32.460 --> 00:06:34.380
<i>Of course she isn't here.</i>

00:06:36.360 --> 00:06:39.000
I hope we get to meet Gunma-chan today.

00:06:39.430 --> 00:06:41.920
I feel like we'll get to!

00:06:42.440 --> 00:06:44.750
Sorry it's just the two of us.

00:06:45.320 --> 00:06:48.380
That's okay. It's nice for a change.

00:06:49.560 --> 00:06:50.650
You're right.

00:06:54.450 --> 00:06:56.700
<i>Hinata and Kokona-chan...</i>

00:06:57.670 --> 00:06:59.420
<i>Of course they aren't here.</i>

00:07:00.270 --> 00:07:01.520
<i>Now, then...</i>

00:07:01.520 --> 00:07:03.510
<i>It's pretty far to Takasaki.</i>

00:07:03.510 --> 00:07:05.670
<i>I think I'll work on my mittens.</i>

00:07:06.020 --> 00:07:08.360
<b>Welcome to Mt. Akagi</b>

00:07:08.360 --> 00:07:10.780
Maebashi Station, Gunma Prefecture

00:07:10.780 --> 00:07:12.360
That was so far.

00:07:12.360 --> 00:07:14.230
And now we take the bus.

00:07:15.650 --> 00:07:16.790
Gunma-chan!

00:07:18.580 --> 00:07:20.120
Over there, too!

00:07:21.870 --> 00:07:23.770
We're off to a good start.

00:07:23.770 --> 00:07:25.150
That's great.

00:07:25.150 --> 00:07:26.000
Yeah!

00:07:29.510 --> 00:07:32.010
Takasaki Station, Gunma Prefecture

00:07:37.360 --> 00:07:41.520
To the right past the gate, 
next to the Dharma...

00:07:48.710 --> 00:07:50.840
Thanks for waiting, Honoka-chan!

00:07:50.840 --> 00:07:52.150
Welcome.

00:07:52.360 --> 00:07:53.790
I brought this for you.

00:07:53.790 --> 00:07:54.910
It's baumkuchen.

00:07:55.070 --> 00:07:56.200
Thanks.

00:07:57.050 --> 00:07:58.170
What's wrong?

00:07:58.170 --> 00:08:00.160
You don't like baumkuchen?

00:08:00.520 --> 00:08:01.600
I do.

00:08:01.600 --> 00:08:03.450
It's not that.

00:08:03.450 --> 00:08:04.170
Um...

00:08:05.280 --> 00:08:09.190
My brother came along.

00:08:11.250 --> 00:08:13.300
<i>Ah.</i>

00:08:16.640 --> 00:08:19.200
I told him we'd take the bus, but...

00:08:19.200 --> 00:08:21.020
This is a lot easier than taking the bus.

00:08:21.230 --> 00:08:22.480
Well, yeah, but...

00:08:22.480 --> 00:08:23.470
What?

00:08:23.470 --> 00:08:27.900
You're always like, "Take 
me for a drive, Onii-chan!"

00:08:27.900 --> 00:08:30.420
I-I've never said that!

00:08:31.410 --> 00:08:32.780
Shut up and drive!

00:08:33.520 --> 00:08:34.400
Jeez...

00:08:35.750 --> 00:08:37.780
<i>Honoka-chan's so cute.</i>

00:08:37.780 --> 00:08:40.040
<b>Bus Station</b>

00:08:37.780 --> 00:08:40.040
<b>Mt. Akagi Cavern</b>

00:08:40.040 --> 00:08:43.040
<b>Rhododendron Path       Kanto Social Road</b>

00:08:40.840 --> 00:08:43.040
We're here!

00:08:43.360 --> 00:08:46.460
Did you get carsick on the 
winding mountain path?

00:08:46.460 --> 00:08:47.590
I'm all right.

00:08:48.020 --> 00:08:49.850
That's Jizoudake.

00:08:50.690 --> 00:08:53.560
I thought we were climbing Mt. Akagi.

00:08:53.970 --> 00:08:57.300
<b>Teach me, Kaede-san!</b>

00:08:56.650 --> 00:08:57.840
Bow.

00:08:57.850 --> 00:09:00.640
Actually, Mt. Akagi is

00:09:00.060 --> 00:09:08.810
<b>Mt. Kurobi</b>

00:09:00.060 --> 00:09:08.810
<b>Mt. Komagatake</b>

00:09:00.060 --> 00:09:08.810
<b>Currently here</b>

00:09:00.060 --> 00:09:08.810
<b>Suzugatake</b>

00:09:00.060 --> 00:09:08.810
<b>Mt. Choushichirou</b>

00:09:00.060 --> 00:09:08.810
<b>Arayama</b>

00:09:00.060 --> 00:09:08.810
<b>Jizoudake</b>

00:09:00.640 --> 00:09:02.910
the general term for several crests,

00:09:02.910 --> 00:09:05.990
including Mt. Kurobi and Komagatake.

00:09:05.990 --> 00:09:08.550
The one they'll be climbing is Jizoudake,

00:09:09.400 --> 00:09:13.010
one of the peaks of Mt. Akagi.

00:09:14.640 --> 00:09:17.670
Is this really the right way?

00:09:17.990 --> 00:09:20.990
<b>To Jizoudake</b>

00:09:17.990 --> 00:09:20.990
<b>To Konuma/Torii Peak</b>

00:09:17.990 --> 00:09:22.960
It says "To Jizoudake," so I'm 
sure this is the right way.

00:09:22.960 --> 00:09:24.460
You're right.

00:09:24.460 --> 00:09:26.870
I'm glad I brought my work gloves.

00:09:27.210 --> 00:09:29.980
All right, let's go!

00:09:29.980 --> 00:09:30.500
Okay!

00:09:36.720 --> 00:09:39.640
All right, Aoi-chan, have fun.

00:09:39.640 --> 00:09:42.140
Th-Thank you.

00:09:48.020 --> 00:09:50.350
Look at all the stone steps.

00:09:51.090 --> 00:09:52.720
I wonder how many there are.

00:09:52.720 --> 00:09:54.320
365.

00:09:54.320 --> 00:09:55.400
That many?

00:09:55.400 --> 00:09:57.320
Apparently they did it that way

00:09:57.810 --> 00:10:01.910
as a wish for it to be busy 
here 365 days a year.

00:10:02.580 --> 00:10:04.720
It's like a mini-hike.

00:10:06.020 --> 00:10:08.020
There's a shrine at the top.

00:10:08.020 --> 00:10:09.380
Let's go there.

00:10:12.470 --> 00:10:13.590
A chicken?

00:10:13.590 --> 00:10:15.470
And this one's a boar?

00:10:16.000 --> 00:10:17.880
Are they the zodiac animals?

00:10:18.260 --> 00:10:20.990
There were apparently twelve 
hot spring hotels here,

00:10:20.990 --> 00:10:23.850
and the zodiac animals
served as their emblems.

00:10:23.850 --> 00:10:26.540
Wow, you know a lot, Honoka-chan.

00:10:26.540 --> 00:10:28.880
Well, I come here a lot.

00:10:28.880 --> 00:10:31.100
I hope we find more zodiacs animals.

00:10:31.460 --> 00:10:33.380
It's cloudy today,

00:10:34.110 --> 00:10:39.110
but if it were clear, you could see 
Mt. Otaka and Mt. Tanigawa from here.

00:10:39.280 --> 00:10:40.640
Really?

00:10:40.640 --> 00:10:43.080
I wonder where Mt. Akagi is.

00:10:43.080 --> 00:10:45.970
Mt. Akagi is... this way.

00:10:48.940 --> 00:10:50.870
Hinata-chan and Kokona-chan?

00:10:50.870 --> 00:10:51.740
Yeah.

00:10:51.740 --> 00:10:54.000
I'm wondering if they might 
be climbing about now.

00:10:54.390 --> 00:10:56.870
Mt. Akagi's pretty, too.

00:10:56.870 --> 00:10:58.130
Let's go there sometime.

00:10:58.130 --> 00:11:00.630
<b>Liquor</b>

00:10:58.300 --> 00:11:00.180
Yeah, we should.

00:11:03.640 --> 00:11:05.890
<b>World 
Folk Art</b>

00:11:03.640 --> 00:11:05.890
<b>General 
Japanese 
Shop</b>

00:11:06.200 --> 00:11:09.390
Honoka-chan, can we take a look in there?

00:11:09.390 --> 00:11:10.980
<b>Japanese 
Shop 
Yokocho</b>

00:11:10.980 --> 00:11:12.010
Of course.

00:11:12.010 --> 00:11:13.480
We can take our time.

00:11:19.540 --> 00:11:21.070
What is this?

00:11:21.070 --> 00:11:22.740
Is this really a hiking trail?

00:11:23.370 --> 00:11:25.820
It's harder than I thought.

00:11:25.820 --> 00:11:28.060
It's slippery, too.

00:11:28.060 --> 00:11:29.370
Be careful.

00:11:29.370 --> 00:11:31.250
Yes, you too.

00:11:32.080 --> 00:11:35.250
<i>Aoi might not have made it up here.</i>

00:11:35.750 --> 00:11:39.600
I have a feeling it'll level out a bit soon.

00:11:39.600 --> 00:11:41.520
Let's take a break when it does.

00:11:41.520 --> 00:11:42.710
Yeah.

00:11:42.710 --> 00:11:44.090
Just a little more.

00:11:44.090 --> 00:11:46.220
Fight, mountain girls!

00:11:46.220 --> 00:11:47.260
Yeah!

00:11:48.410 --> 00:11:51.160
<i>It would have been rough 
if Aoi had been here.</i>

00:11:51.160 --> 00:11:53.120
<i>So it's all good.</i>

00:11:53.440 --> 00:11:54.750
<i>Yup, yup.</i>

00:11:56.110 --> 00:11:59.940
<b>To Be Continued</b>
